WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.140
- [announcer] If you've
been itching for a vacation,

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:03.440
you're not alone.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.270
Summer holiday travel has
surged to levels not seen

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.840
since before the COVID 19 pandemic.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.290
The consumer price index,

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.710
which is the benchmark
measure of inflation

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:14.920
rose 0.9% in June.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.820
The largest one month increase since 2008.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.600
Vacation related expenses weren't spared.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.240
Prices increased for everything

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.190
from new cameras and swimsuits

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.466
to rental cars and hotel rooms.

00:00:26.466 --> 00:00:29.870
- We're just, have this
kind of collective need

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.380
to get out and about.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.960
- [announcer] Experts say price increases

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:36.550
reflect an economy on the
upswing from pandemic lows.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.060
But higher demand has made
some vacation essentials

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.330
harder to come by.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.250
Here's why that is, in some strategies

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.053
to help avoid the sticker shock.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:46.620
As lockdowns have eased,

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.410
summer holiday travel has
surged both in the air

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.100
and on the ground.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:54.010
AAA says more than 47
million people traveled

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:56.270
over the 4th of July holiday weekend,

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:58.610
which is 40% more than last year.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.670
But US Air travel is still recovering

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:04.270
after the pandemic drove
it to a virtual standstill.

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:07.040
Much of the recovery lag has
to do with the slow return

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.320
of business travel.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:09.650
However, airlines prepared

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:12.130
for an almost normal schedule
of flights this summer

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:14.440
as leisure travel demand returned.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.770
Contributing to airfare
increasing nearly 25%

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:18.943
since last year.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.727
If you're looking for cheaper airfare,

00:01:21.727 --> 00:01:23.940
"WSJ" Travel Editor, Deborah Dunn

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.400
suggest switching up when you fly.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.410
- The key to finding
less expensive airfare,

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:31.400
is to be really flexible.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.820
Not just traveling on a weekend

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.820
or traveling from a Saturday to Sunday,

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:40.710
but I would look at the price difference

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.010
if you fly on a Tuesday or Wednesday.

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:44.350
- [announcer] But once
you're all booked in

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:46.280
and touchdown at your destination,

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:48.400
you still may hit those higher prices.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.910
Vehicle rental prices are
up over 87% from a year ago.

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:56.410
The simple reason is that
rental companies have less cars.

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:59.170
Smaller rental fleets had one big issue.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:02.850
Summer demand surged
over 300% in some cities,

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.400
according to KAYAK.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.610
This has led some
travelers being turned away

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:09.150
at the rental counter because
there aren't enough cars

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.300
on the lot.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.880
And with a semiconductor shortage,

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.100
continuing to hamper new car production,

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.800
some analysts think it
will be well into 2022

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.067
before fleet supplies are
enough to meet demand.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:22.908
- Book months and months ahead.

00:02:22.908 --> 00:02:27.908
And I wouldn't book a
non-refundable reservation.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:33.080
The other possibility is to
look at picking up a car in town

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:34.900
rather than in the airport,

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.790
you'll have to take an
Uber from the airport,

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:40.360
but it's still day to day,
probably a better deal.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.660
- [narrator] Those with
their own set of wheels

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.970
could count themselves lucky

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:45.670
if they weren't facing the
steepest gasoline prices

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:47.230
in nearly seven years

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.960
as gas shortages have
plagued many regions.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.070
The Colonial Pipeline cyber attack in May

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:55.087
led to East Coast shortages
right before the summer season.

00:02:55.087 --> 00:02:57.590
And some regions of the
country have had a hard time

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:00.910
restocking gas stations because
of a lack of truck drivers.

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:03.410
Many of whom had been laid
off during the pandemic,

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.620
according to analysts.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:08.430
And the high prices, aren't
restricted to travel expenses.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.293
Men's and women's swimwear prices were up

00:03:10.293 --> 00:03:12.483
1.4 and 5.5% respectively,

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:16.710
which analysts attribute
to pent-up vacation demand.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.170
Demand outpacing supply

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:20.810
has hit other vacation essentials as well.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:24.837
Like cameras, which have
risen in price by almost 6%.

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:27.370
And depending on where
your head hits the pillow,

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:29.810
you could be paying
more for accommodations.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:33.100
Room rates have recovered
to pre pandemic levels.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.710
But the slow return of business travel

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:36.840
has kept occupancy rates slightly lower

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.896
than before the pandemic
according to analysts.

00:03:39.896 --> 00:03:42.750
And while demand may be high
in traditional destinations

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.220
like Florida and Hawaii,

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.290
experts say price
increases are being driven

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.540
by vacationers booking
bigger accommodations

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.630
that may be off the beaten path.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.900
Travelers are opting
for larger hotel suites

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.260
or entire rental houses

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:56.720
to accommodate families
vacationing together.

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:58.130
And according to AirDNA,

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:01.690
which tracks short-term rental
prices of Airbnb and Vrbo,

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:04.790
demand in small cities in
rural locations has surged

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:07.620
over 51% since 2019.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.840
The current vacation
season is being defined

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:11.540
by an economy in recovery

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:14.200
and a population desperate for some RnR,

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.810
even if it puts a dent in their wallets.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.320
- Be flexible about where you're gonna go,

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.070
when you're gonna go, how
long you're gonna stay.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:25.500
Flexibility, I think is the
operative word this summer.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.320
The last thing you wanna be
is stressed out on vacation.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:30.290
- But if prices continue to rise,

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:33.169
a stress-free vacation
may be harder to come by.

00:04:33.169 --> 00:04:35.752
(gentle music)

